B.J1=new A.bh(B.es,["RT-TEC: Real-Time Trade Eligibility Classifier","Sub-10ms ML system for real-time trade decisions","assets/images/RT_TEC.png","Developed a production-grade, real-time trading decision system using FastAPI and NVIDIA Triton for GPU-accelerated ML inference. The system determines trade eligibility in milliseconds, ensuring compliance and safety in high-frequency trading environments.","Key features include sub-10ms latency, fail-safe design, multi-layer validation, and comprehensive audit trails using PostgreSQL. The architecture incorporates Feast and Redis for real-time feature serving, RedPanda for market data ingestion, and Prometheus with Grafana for monitoring. The system supports hot-swappable models, A/B testing, and version management, making it ideal for high-frequency trading firms and algorithmic trading platforms.",B.Hh,"https://github.com/Aashay7/RT-TEC","Personal Project / Lead Developer","Jun 2025 - Present","In Progress"],t.yf)
B.Gw=s(["RAG","FastAPI","SQLite","Embeddings","Summarization","Document QA","NLP"],t.s)
B.J_=new A.bh(B.es,["Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) for Finance Applications","Local prototype for document QA and summarization","images/RAGFinance.png","Built a local prototype of a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) system for financial documents using FastAPI and SQLite. The system supports document ingestion, chunking, embedding, retrieval, and summarization, enabling users to ask questions and get concise answers from a corpus of financial texts.","The pipeline includes a demo document ingestion endpoint, recent document listing, and a question-answering interface that retrieves relevant chunks and generates summaries. The system uses sentence-transformers for embeddings and can leverage OpenAI\u2019s API for advanced summarization if an API key is provided. This project showcases the potential of RAG in financial applications, providing a foundation for more complex deployments.",B.Gw,"https://example.com/rag-finance","Personal Project / Lead Developer","Jun 2025 - Present","In Progress"],t.yf)
B.H8=s(["NeRF","3D Reconstruction","TensorFlow","PyTorch","Slurm","NumPy"],t.s)
B.J2=new A.bh(B.es,["3D View Synthesis using NeRF","Neural Radiance Fields for novel view generation","assets/images/NeRFCVPoster.jpeg","Implemented 3D scene reconstruction using volumetric rendering and ray sampling techniques, based on the NeRF paper (https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.08934). Final training on IU\u2019s Carbonate GPU cluster using TensorFlow. Used both PyTorch and TF for experimentation.","This project involved creating a neural network that can generate novel views of a scene from a sparse set of input images. The model learns to represent the scene as a continuous volumetric field, allowing it to synthesize new perspectives by sampling rays through the volume. The implementation was optimized for performance and accuracy, leveraging advanced techniques like positional encoding and hierarchical sampling.",B.H8,"https://example.com/3d-view-synthesis","Lead Developer","Jan 2022 - May 2022","Completed"],t.yf)
B.JS={title:0,description:1,image:2,details:3,additionalDetails:4,tags:5,link:6,role:7,duration:8,status:9,published:10}
